Surprise! The <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/28/apple-new-macbook-pro/">new 14-inch and 16-inch MacBook Pro models with OLED displays</a> have <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/28/illuminated-logo-returns-to-macbook-pro/">a glowing Apple logo</a>, a beloved feature that was phased out a decade ago.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/MacBook-Pro-Glowing-Apple-Logo.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1074267" /><br/>
In a <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jHd_ekvZ_wA">hands-on video</a> shared on his YouTube channel UrAvgConsumer, Judner Aura showed off the glowing Apple logo and revealed that its brightness is tied to the MacBook Pro's display brightness. If you turn up the display brightness, the logo gets brighter, and vice versa. The glowing logo worked the same way on older MacBooks.<br/>
<br/>
Skip ahead to the one-minute mark of the video to see the glowing Apple logo.<br/>
<br/>
